{"id":"8602c564-ec35-450c-86a7-0935bc93aa54","object":"chat.completion","created":1785028767,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    n = len(segments)\\n    if not isinstance(segments, list) or not isinstance(budget, int):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Invalid case structure\\\")\\n    for seg in segments:\\n        if not all(k in seg for k in ('name','importance','minimum','capacity')):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Missing segment fields\\\")\\n    min_sum = sum(seg['minimum'] for seg in segments)\\n    cap_sum = sum(seg['capacity'] for seg in segments)\\n    if budget < min_sum or budget > cap_sum:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Budget out of feasible range\\\")\\n    alloc = [seg['minimum'] for seg in segments]\\n    remaining = budget - min_sum\\n    caps = [seg['capacity'] for seg in segments]\\n    imp = [seg['importance'] for seg in segments]\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_idx = None\\n        best_num = None\\n        best_den = None\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            if alloc[i] >= caps[i]:\\n                continue\\n            num = imp[i]\\n            den = alloc[i] + 1\\n            if best_idx is None:\\n                best_idx = i\\n                best_num = num\\n                best_den = den\\n            else:\\n                lhs = num * best_den\\n                rhs = best_num * den\\n                if lhs > rhs or (lhs == rhs and i < best_idx):\\n                    best_idx = i\\n                    best_num = num\\n                    best_den = den\\n        if best_idx is None:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Allocation stuck\\\")\\n        alloc[best_idx] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    total = sum(alloc)\\n    by_name = {}\\n    for i, seg in enumerate(segments):\\n        by_name[seg['name']] = alloc[i]\\n    return {\\\"allocations\\\": alloc, \\\"by_name\\\": by_name, \\\"total\\\": total}\\n\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to write solve(case) that implements the described algorithm. The case has segments list with name, importance, minimum, capacity; and budget. We need to allocate tokens to meet minimums first, then distribute remaining budget to segments proportionally by importance / (current allocation+1?) Actually description: \"give one token to the segment maximizing importance divided by its next allocated position.\" That suggests a greedy algorithm: while budget left, pick segment with highest importance / (current_allocation + 1) (since next allocated position = current count + 1). But the description says \"importance divided by its next allocated position\". If segment currently has k tokens, next token would be at position k+1, so score = importance / (k+1). That's typical for proportional allocation. Also tie-break by original segment order (index in list). The output: allocations list of integers in same order as segments; by_name dict mapping segment names to their allocation; total sum of allocations.\n\nAlso must raise ValueError if budget < sum(minimum) or budget > sum(capacity). But careful: budget is exact total? The problem says \"Reject budgets below the quota sum or above total capacity\". So if budget < sum(minimum) or budget > sum(capacity), raise ValueError. Also if budget is exactly sum(minimum) then no extra tokens. If budget is exactly sum(capacity) then allocate all capacity.\n\nImplementation steps:\n1. Validate case has required fields: segments list, budget integer. Each segment must have name (string), importance (int), minimum (int), capacity (int). We can assume valid from fixtures but we should check for safety.\n2. Compute min_sum = sum(seg['minimum'] for seg in segments)\n3. Compute cap_sum = sum(seg['capacity'] for seg in segments)\n4. If budget < min_sum or budget > cap_sum: raise ValueError\n5. Initialize allocations = [seg['minimum'] for seg in segments]; remaining = budget - min_sum\n6. While remaining > 0:\n   - For each segment index i, compute score = seg['importance'] / (allocations[i] + 1) only if allocations[i] < seg['capacity'] (since cannot exceed capacity). Actually we must cap; if a segment is at capacity, it cannot receive more. So ignore those.\n   - Choose segment with max score; if tie, choose lower index (original order). It's important to use stable tie break: break equal priorities by original segment order. Since we iterate i from 0, we can keep track of best index and best score, and if score equals best score and index is lower? Actually we want to pick first among ties? The description says \"Break equal priorities by original segment order.\" Typically that means if two have same score, the one earlier in list gets priority. So we can do: if score > best_score or (score == best_score and i < best_index) then update.\n   - Increment allocations[best_index] by 1, decrement remaining.\n7. After loop, compute total = sum(allocations)\n8. Build by_name dict: for i, seg in enumerate(segments): by_name[seg['name']] = allocations[i]\n9. Return {\"allocations\": allocations, \"by_name\": by_name, \"total\": total}\n\nEdge: ensure we don't exceed capacity: in loop, only consider segments not at capacity. Also need to handle case where no segment can take more but remaining>0? That shouldn't happen because budget <= total capacity and we start from min, so if budget = total capacity, we will allocate all remaining exactly to fill capacities. If budget < total capacity, we stop when remaining=0. So loop will end.\n\nWe must not mutate case. We'll create new list for allocations, copy segment data if needed.\n\nNow produce the JSON output with single key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a JSON string. Must escape all special characters: newlines as \\n, backslashes as \\\\, quotes as \\\". Also ensure no Markdown fenced code. The entire response should be a JSON object with one key \"implementation\". So final output: {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\\n\"}\n\nLet's write the code carefully. We'll include error handling with ValueError. Ensure Python version compatibility (standard library only). No imports needed.\n\nWe'll define solve(case) that returns dictionary. Note: case is the payload object, not the whole fixture row. It has segments and budget. We'll assume it's a dict.\n\nWrite the function body.\n\nPossible improvements: use integer arithmetic? Scores are fractions; we can compare using cross multiplication to avoid floating point errors: compare a/b vs c/d as a*d vs c*b. But importance and allocations+1 are integers. However, we need to handle ties exactly. Using floats may have precision issues but for given fixtures sizes likely fine. But safer to use rational comparison: for each segment, we compute numerator = importance, denominator = allocations[i]+1, then compare candidate_score_num * best_denom vs best_score_num * candidate_denom. We'll keep best_score_num, best_score_den as integers. We'll also store best_index.\n\nImplementation:\n\n```\ndef solve(case):\n    segments = case['segments']\n    budget = case['budget']\n    n = len(segments)\n    # Validate\n    if not isinstance(segments, list) or not isinstance(budget, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid case structure\")\n    for seg in segments:\n        if not all(k in seg for k in ('name','importance','minimum','capacity')):\n            raise ValueError(\"Missing segment fields\")\n    min_sum = sum(seg['minimum'] for seg in segments)\n    cap_sum = sum(seg['capacity'] for seg in segments)\n    if budget < min_sum or budget > cap_sum:\n        raise ValueError(\"Budget out of feasible range\")\n    alloc = [seg['minimum'] for seg in segments]\n    remaining = budget - min_sum\n    # Precompute capacities and importance\n    caps = [seg['capacity'] for seg in segments]\n    imp = [seg['importance'] for seg in segments]\n    while remaining > 0:\n        best_idx = None\n        best_num = None\n        best_den = None\n        for i in range(n):\n            if alloc[i] >= caps[i]:\n                continue\n            # score = imp[i] / (alloc[i] + 1)\n            num = imp[i]\n            den = alloc[i] + 1\n            if best_idx is None:\n                best_idx = i\n                best_num = num\n                best_den = den\n            else:\n                # compare num/den vs best_num/best_den\n                # num * best_den > best_num * den ? if true then better\n                lhs = num * best_den\n                rhs = best_num * den\n                if lhs > rhs or (lhs == rhs and i < best_idx):\n                    # if tie, earlier index gets priority (i < best_idx means earlier)\n                    best_idx = i\n                    best_num = num\n                    best_den = den\n        if best_idx is None:\n            # should not happen because budget <= cap_sum and remaining > 0, but just in case\n            raise ValueError(\"Allocation stuck\")\n        alloc[best_idx] += 1\n        remaining -= 1\n    total = sum(alloc)\n    by_name = {}\n    for i, seg in enumerate(segments):\n        by_name[seg['name']] = alloc[i]\n    return {\"allocations\": alloc, \"by_name\": by_name, \"total\": total}\n```\n\nThat's it.\n\nNow we need to output as JSON string inside \"implementation\". We'll write the Python code as a string, escaping appropriately.\n\nWe'll produce the final JSON response."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1499,"completion_tokens":2113,"total_tokens":3612,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1408},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1642},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1408,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":91},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}